From de16088cd3fd133deb915d3e1e9f454362928cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:20:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/63] efi/arm: boot the NVIDIA Tegra 2 of the Toshiba AC100

- translate device tree addresses through all parent buses
- keep the frame buffer out of the kernel's free memory
- let a Cortex-A9 MPCore take part in coherency
- stop the Tegra20 USB controllers the firmware left running
- switch the radios of rfkill-gpio nodes on, and the AC100 wireless
  module, which has no rfkill node
- pass the Tegra PMC, RTC, DVC I2C, PL310 and private timer to the kernel
- start the other CPUs through PSCI, or through the flow controller of
  the Tegra 2, and hand them over to the kernel
- find the boot partitions of a disk with only the backup GPT

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
